      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The concept of \"election security\" is a balance between robust, real-time security and the practical need to resolve complex legal and procedural claims after the fact. While the timeline for deeply complex legal or systemic reviews can indeed be long, the primary function of the election process is to secure the vote *on election day*, not to definitively litigate all potential after-the-fact claims.",
      "source": "target",
